     * when did a fix exist" and falls back to the CVE date only when no remediation
     * date is published, while this one always means "when was the CVE disclosed".
     * Also distinct from [firstSeenAt], which is when *we* first detected it — the
     * three routinely differ by years, and conflating them is what made a 2023 CVE
     * indistinguishable from a 2025 one in the UI.
     *
     * Display and reporting only; the SLA anchor remains [firstSeenAt] (or the
     * patch date when `secman.vulnerability.use-patch-publication-date` is on).
